# tenant_migrations.manifest
#
# Byte-identical record of every TENANT_MIGRATIONS entry that has ever shipped.
# Format: <version>: <description>   (blank lines and # comments ignored)
#
# RULES (enforced by tenant_migrations_obey_append_only_manifest test):
#   1. Lines below this header are APPEND-ONLY. Never edit, never reorder,
#      never remove a line that has already shipped.
#   2. To add a new tenant migration: append a new (version, description)
#      line at the END here AND add the matching TenantMigration entry at the
#      end of TENANT_MIGRATIONS in tenant_migrations.rs. Both files must move
#      together in the same commit.
#   3. To change behavior for an already-published version, add a NEW
#      migration with the next higher version number; do NOT edit the old entry.
#
# History (2026-05-22, Patch 20): position v48 was reaffected at the VOCSAP
# merge of upstream commits d71342e + a0880ee; v55 re-applies the missing
# ALTERs idempotently. See git log.
#
# History (2026-05-31, merge upstream aa6a0bec): DOCUMENTED DISCONTINUITY. The
# upstream merge took tenant versions v55-v59 for its *_user_id_readd chain,
# colliding with the VOCSAP v55-v59 (supervisor_injections_repair,
# approvals_gate_id, conversations_space_id, structured_facts_unique_index,
# structured_facts_extraction_source). The VOCSAP migrations were renumbered to
# v72-v76 (appended after upstream max v71). Their bodies are idempotent
# (table_has_column / CREATE [UNIQUE] INDEX IF NOT EXISTS) so re-running them
# under the new numbers is a NO-OP on the single existing deployment (LXC 121,
# already at v55-v59). This manifest was REGENERATED from the merged array;
# lines v55-v59 now carry the upstream descriptions. This is the only
# intentional break of the byte-identical rule, tied to this merge.

